# Branches

Running managers update from `main` (they read `VERSION` there and pull it), so `main` only moves when the
maintainer merges a release pull request on GitHub.

| Branch | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `changes/unreleased` | Everything not released yet. Exists only while there are unreleased changes. |
| `version/X.Y.Z` | One release: `changes/unreleased` renamed, plus the version bump and changelog. |
| `main` | Released versions only. Never commit or push to it directly unless the user says so. |

## Day to day

- Before changing anything, check out `changes/unreleased`. If it does not exist yet, create it from an up-to-date
  `main` and push it:

  ```bash
  git switch main && git pull --ff-only
  git switch -c changes/unreleased && git push -u origin changes/unreleased
  ```

- If a `version/X.Y.Z` pull request is still open, ask the user to merge it first, so the new branch starts from
  the released `main`.
- Stay on `changes/unreleased` until a release; commit and push there. Do not open pull requests for it.
- User-visible changes go under **Unreleased** in `CHANGELOG.md`, as before.

## Releasing X.Y.Z (only with a number the user gave; see the `manager-release` skill)

```bash
V=1.2.3
git switch changes/unreleased && git pull --ff-only
git branch -m changes/unreleased "version/$V"
git push -u origin "version/$V" && git push origin --delete changes/unreleased
# bump VERSION/package files, move CHANGELOG Unreleased to $V, npm run check && npm test
git commit -am "Version $V" && git push
git tag "v$V" && git push origin "v$V"
gh release create "v$V" --verify-tag --title "$V" --notes-file /tmp/notes.md --latest
gh pr create --base main --head "version/$V" --title "Version $V" --body-file /tmp/notes.md
```

- The maintainer merges the pull request by hand on GitHub; never merge it yourself. Users get the update only
  after that merge.
- Do not create a new `changes/unreleased` after a release; it is created from `main` when the next change starts.
